**Issue**: #271
**Date**: 2026-08-26
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

@issue-271 @bug @steering-runtime
Feature: Load project steering without snippet byte bounds
  Project-owned steering guidance must be able to grow without blocking prompt
  construction, while plugin catalog fragments retain explicit safety bounds.

  Scenario: Worker start loads unbounded project snippets
    Given this repository has registered project steering snippets
    And a project snippet body exceeds its former byte bound
    When the worker start prompt is constructed for issue 102
    Then prompt construction returns a non-empty string
    And no "byte_bound_exceeded" or "worker_prompt_failed" error is raised

  Scenario: Project manifest snippets omit byteBound
    Given a valid project steering manifest
    When the steering runtime loads its snippet records
    Then each normalized snippet contains "id", "path", "consumers", "slot", and "order"
    And no normalized or repository snippet contains "byteBound"

  Scenario: Legacy project byteBound is ignored
    Given a project manifest snippet has "byteBound" 1
    And its body is longer than 1 byte
    When the project runtime and default prompt registry load it
    Then loading and registration succeed
    And the project prompt fragment has no "byteBound" property
    And its consumer prompt renders the snippet body

  Scenario: Plugin catalog bounds remain enforced
    Given a plugin fragment has "byteBound" 1
    And its body is longer than 1 byte
    When the prompt registry registers the plugin fragment
    Then registration fails with "byte_bound_exceeded"

  Scenario: Initialize and migrate plans omit byteBound
    Given project steering is initialized or detected for migration
    When the candidate steering manifest is written
    Then every snippet record omits "byteBound"
    And each snippet retains its id, path, consumers, slot, and order
